{"id": "EUVD-2026-103581", "enisaUuid": "115ef2df-e161-34db-80f2-b07844c8e203", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwriteback: report a Tasks-RCU quiescent state per cgwb drain pass\n\ncleanup_offline_cgwbs_workfn() drains a dying cgwb by calling\ncleanup_offline_cgwb() until it returns false, with a cond_resched()\nbetween passes.  On a CONFIG_PREEMPTION kernel that cond_resched() does\nnothing: _cond_resched() is a plain \"return 0\", and under PREEMPT_DYNAMIC\nthe full and lazy modes disable it.  Since commit 7dadeaa6e851 (\"sched:\nFurther restrict the preemption modes\") those are the only two models on\nthe architectures with PREEMPT_LAZY support, arm64 and x86 among them, so\nthe drain loop never reports a Tasks-RCU quiescent state.\n\nA worker draining a cgwb with millions of attached inodes runs for\nminutes.  On a 6.18 arm64 host in lazy mode the cgwb worker drained one\ndying cgroup's writeback domain for over 11 minutes.  A BPF program unlink\n(bpf_trampoline_unlink_prog -> bpf_trampoline_update ->\nunregister_ftrace_direct -> ftrace_shutdown -> synchronize_rcu_tasks())\nwaited on that grace period while holding the trampoline mutex, 42 tasks\nqueued behind it in D state, and the hung task detector fired at 614 s and\npanicked the host.  Any BPF or ftrace detach during a long drain inherits\nthe drain's length.\n\nFix this by calling cond_resched_tasks_rcu_qs() so we do not stall out\nanybody who calls sycnrhonize_rcu_tasks().  We put this in a do { } while\nloop because if we have many small cgroups cleanup_offline_cgwb() will\nreturn false and we will never call cond_resched_tasks_rcu_qs(), creating\nthe same problem.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:19", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/863049b4018237d1590cd13b16e9fe9c0faad2c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/42462b5bb0dec57db7f85d0f77655c737d45754d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ebf1555ad2821be06f87a88ffd9a2cab8d2200e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4eb889649eaf65f4a5727b04ba1c017b7d05bb16", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd3bf32279df98751364b3609eb100a3e42f253b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/260f586a80e7f624dd7f069898a75a904f34d373", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/407a5d205179a4ab186571b0e16ec42725dc77bc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hq8j-r79p-42p5", "CVE-2026-98536"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0d764dea-266c-3a9f-8814-d236ba3e109a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "27bbe060-3c90-384b-b2aa-a1a8ba41394e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "4c7e7bd6-f8b7-335c-869e-bf06eee93560", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c22d70a162d3cc177282c4487be4d54876ca55c8 <4eb889649eaf65f4a5727b04ba1c017b7d05bb16"}, {"id": "56ca52d3-ab69-32bc-8413-e8110551baa2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c22d70a162d3cc177282c4487be4d54876ca55c8 <407a5d205179a4ab186571b0e16ec42725dc77bc"}, {"id": "62049442-ad1a-306b-b8eb-04214b0b92d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "6b811c72-4d90-3414-9c79-41ff6010e9d8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c22d70a162d3cc177282c4487be4d54876ca55c8 <42462b5bb0dec57db7f85d0f77655c737d45754d"}, {"id": "85da6d89-cef3-30bb-bada-a0f776b3ce26", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c22d70a162d3cc177282c4487be4d54876ca55c8 <260f586a80e7f624dd7f069898a75a904f34d373"}, {"id": "86d094a5-9a61-3f59-ac9d-e77973dc4bfb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "96d3243c-e8de-398a-8ef8-573d95f47c7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "a42cbc75-74ae-397b-a38b-a9c50776d512", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c22d70a162d3cc177282c4487be4d54876ca55c8 <fd3bf32279df98751364b3609eb100a3e42f253b"}, {"id": "b14da07e-3d96-37a0-abd1-895482fb72c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "d74ee61c-cc1f-3b94-9aa1-7deb2cdd9e22", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "dc302532-1289-35fb-bcab-23f647ac58d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.14"}, {"id": "f7a33c79-702f-3224-8143-f0a65cefc7b8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c22d70a162d3cc177282c4487be4d54876ca55c8 <863049b4018237d1590cd13b16e9fe9c0faad2c6"}, {"id": "fc4220cb-f19e-309d-b990-20fe89eeb0c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c22d70a162d3cc177282c4487be4d54876ca55c8 <ebf1555ad2821be06f87a88ffd9a2cab8d2200e1"}, {"id": "fc48a1ff-550a-3e34-9a3c-e3ba0fba44df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6fa67147-b33f-3d6a-b4dc-6b4da1d4b11b", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}